  offerDialogue:
    name: Vance
    sentences:
    - Vehicles from the factory can already reach the other side.
    - The issue is that the road takes them all the way around the canyon.
    - 'They end up traveling much farther than they need to. '
    - A bridge here would give them a much more direct route.
    - "This crossing will carry a heavier vehicle than the ones you\u2019ve handled
      before."
    - <b><#E09500>As that weight moves across, different parts of the bridge may
      respond in different ways<#E09500></b>.
    - <b><#E09500>Pay attention to how the structural members behave during the test<#E09500></b>.
    - Watch how they work together as the vehicle crosses.
    - "If you\u2019re ready, I can give you the contract."
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Vance
    sentences: []
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Vance
    sentences:
    - 'Take your time with the design.

'
    - Keep an eye on how the different parts of the bridge respond during the test.
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Vance
    sentences:
    - "Now that\u2019s a shortcut."
    - Vehicles from the factory can head straight through instead of taking the long
      way around the canyon.
    - That should save everyone using this route a lot of travel time.
